Goldenland AI Assist workflow & collaboration (USER PREFERENCE — missing it gets called out): per implement ticket, load originating issue via gh, read its 'Parent' + acceptance criteria first. Mandatory two-axis code review (standards + spec) via parallel delegate/reviewer sub-agents before commit — no specialized code-review subagent exists; pass explicit shell diff instructions (`git diff <fixed-point>...HEAD`, `git log <fixed-point>..HEAD`); pin fixed point per-ticket from commit graph (feature commit's parent SHA). Drift failure mode: sub-agents reviewed ticket #18 slug/analytics instead of the working-tree diff — write the exact diff to a file, constrain agents hard, verify findings against the actual changeset. Ledger to docs/agents/reviews/<issue>.md: fixed point, spec/standards sources, findings table (finding/axis/classification/disposition); verify findings against HEAD before writing (later batch tickets may already fix them). Delete dead code only with zero references at HEAD, excluding .pi-subagents/ and docs/agents/reviews/. Never skip Resolve: `gh issue close` with summary (commit SHA, test results, ledger path) + context-pointer comment on #1's 'Implementation Decisions'. Batched close-outs: 2 axes × N tickets as parallel sub-agents; trust nothing from completion events (truncated aggregates, transient child failures) — inspect .pi-subagents/artifacts/ raw outputs, re-run failed children. Testing: behavior-changing fixes must update tests encoding the old contract (GA4 health tests → ga4_key_events); regression tests alongside existing (DomainBlacklistServiceTest, Ga4HealthTest). Model behavior: free models work at $0; only negative balance blocks (402s everything, incl. :free) until topped up; free variants report 0/0 pricing in /models so budget guard skips them; OpenRouter bills post-completion so balance can dip negative — low-credit gate is warnings-only, never a block (cliff ADR 0009's warning threshold). Collaboration: stress-test via /grill-with-docs and /grilling; during grilling back design decisions with live facts (researcher subagent fetches primary sources) before locking the tree; prefers 'design tree' rounds on the current frontier; /wait-wait → re-pitch in ASD-STE100 + ubiquitous language from CONTEXT.md. Model selection: AI Settings → 'Global model chain' → 'OpenRouter generation policy' (reorderable, live catalog filtered to image-input + structured-output); free models must be explicitly in chain for no-credit fallback. Primary agent delegates context-heavy verifiable work; keeps user-facing decisions, orchestration, synthesis, final verification. Global AGENTS.md stays generic/reusable; vendor-specific flows (Matt Pocock's skills) go in their own SKILL.md files. <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-09 -->
