Pi environment & tool quirks: Pi auto-loads every .ts/.js directly in ~/.pi/agent/extensions/ (and cwd/.pi/extensions/) in addition to the settings.json 'extensions' array; subdirs load only with index.ts or package.json carrying pi.extensions — disable an extension by moving it to a subdir (e.g. extensions/retired/). prime-tui patches: reapply `bash ~/.pi/agent/prime-tui/apply-patches.sh` after any npm update of pi-coding-agent; patched copies live in ~/.pi/agent/prime-tui/patched/. prime-header.ts: splash header (logo + version/model/cwd/counts) via ctx.ui.setHeader on session_start. Patched TUI quirks: settings-list.js — Space always toggles the selected option and strips spaces from search input; interactive-mode.js — fullscreen quit fixed via TUI stop with preserveScreen: true; editor.js — regular-mode overflow crash (TuiMainScreen.doRender throws on lines wider than the terminal, writes pi-crash.log) caused by '> ' prompt drawn inside left padding without shrinking the text budget; fullscreen never checks, so only regular mode crashes. pi-subagents extension (Nico Bailon): intercom bridge, 8 builtin agents, 35 skills, unlimited spawn budget. Tool quirk: perl-regex-style text replacements can swallow trailing characters (e.g. a semicolon) — always verify syntax after such a fix. <!-- created=2026-08-08, last=2026-08-08 -->
